<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  PRODUCT_SPEC 15 — release builds reject cleartext traffic.

  `cleartextTrafficPermitted="false"` with no domain exceptions, and it stays that way. Open decision
  24.13 — whether a release build may reach a cleartext LAN server — is resolved as **no**, and
  ADR-0009 records why: Android cannot express a *per-server* exception, so the only lever available
  would drop the guarantee for every host in order to serve one.

  Debug builds override this file with `app/src/debug/res/xml/network_security_config.xml`, which does
  permit cleartext. That is where a LAN-only `http://` server is reachable.

  There is intentionally no `<trust-anchors>` override anywhere in this file. PRODUCT_SPEC AUTH-001
  forbids a "trust all certificates" mode, and a debug-only trust anchor is the usual way one gets
  added by accident.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" />
</network-security-config>
